		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T06:21:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				105,
				19
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Enforce telemetry kill-switch and bridge event replay for bundled profiles\n\nExtend the Sky bridge and bundled workbench entry points to honor the master `Capture` and `Report` environment variables, ensuring PostHog and OTLP telemetry can be globally disabled alongside the `Disable` polyfill kill-switch. Update `OTELBridge.ts` and `PostHogBridge.ts` to gate initialization on these flags and suppress built-in unhandled error capture to avoid duplicate null-property events.\n\nAdd the `sky:replay-events` invocation at the end of `InstallSkyBridge` for bundled profiles to drain pending Mountain events (tree-view registrations, SCM providers, terminal buffers) that occur during the Cocoon activation cascade, preventing event loss when listeners attach late. Update `SkyBridge.ts` to correctly handle `TauriChannel` method interception and search-result mapping shapes. Apply consistent PascalCase formatting and multiline brace styles across entry scripts, smoke tests, and Astro layouts to align with project standards.\n\nThis ensures robust event delivery during startup, accurate diagnostics via telemetry gates, and formatting consistency across the bundled editor profiles.",
			"SHA": "c636f0e8dc34b688a612a38dd4380ac7ec94189e"
		}
	],
